# apt-cache — query the APT package index

## Search for packages

```sh
apt-cache search "whatever"
```

## Display package records

```sh
apt-cache show pkg
```

## Reverse dependencies (what needs this package?)

```sh
apt-cache rdepends package_name
```

## Versions plus forward and reverse dependencies

```sh
apt-cache showpkg package_name
```

## Real-world: check what would break before removing a library

```sh
apt-cache rdepends --installed libssl3
```

## Real-world: compare candidate vs installed version

```sh
apt-cache policy nginx
```

| Command  | What it shows                       |
| -------- | ----------------------------------- |
| search   | name/description matches            |
| show     | full package record                 |
| policy   | installed vs candidate + origin     |
| rdepends | reverse dependencies                |
| depends  | forward dependencies                |
